bility\nEligibility\nInformation for Reference Writers\nHolistic Admission\nCost and Aid\nCost and Aid\nExternal Scholarship Opportunities\nDeadlines\nApply\nFAQ\nContract Students\nAdmission Events\nAdmission Events\nInformation Sessions\nContact Admissions\nDVM Program\nDVM Program\nProgram Overview\nProgram Overview\nCurriculum Focus Areas\nClinical Competencies\nExtramural Studies\nInternational Programs\nLicensing Requirements\nWithdrawal\nCurriculum\nAdvising\nCombined Degree Programs\nUndergraduate Scholar Programs\nClinical Rotations for Visiting DVM Students\nOffice of Student Affairs and Education\nOffice of Student Affairs and Education\nThe Office of Student Affairs\nThe Office of Professional Education and Admissions\nCounseling\nAccreditation\nClinical Communications\nClinical Communications\nSimulated Clients\nContact Us\nGraduate Program\nGraduate Program\nCell Biology\nInfection and Immunity\nNeurosciences\nPopulation and Global Health\nAffiliated Training Programs\nUndergraduate Engagement\nStudent Experience\nStudent Experience\nStudent Development\nStudent Enrichment\nCareer Preparation\nCounseling Services\nFinancial Wellness\nResearch\nResearch\nAreas of Emphasis\nAreas of Emphasis\nBiological Barriers\nComputational Biology and Bioinformatics\nDevelopmental Biology\nGastroenterology\nGenetics\nGlobal Health\nImmunology\nInfectious Disease\nNeurobiology\nPharmacology\nRegenerative Medicine\nSpontaneous Animal Disease Models\nResearch Centers, Consortia and Institutes\nDiagnostic and Research Labs\nDiagnostic and Research Labs\nResearch Labs\nBiosafety Level 3 (BSL3) Biocontainment Facility\nClinical Sciences Lab\nClinical Sciences Lab\nCanine Spinal Cord Injury\nCompanion Animal Epilepsy\nTranslational Research in Pain (TRiP)\nEquine Orthopedic Research\nIntestinal Pathogens Research\nIntestinal Regenerative Medicine\nIntracellular Pathogens Research\nK9/Feline Oncology Diagnostic Lab\nLeukocyte Biology\nTritrichomonas Diagnostic Laboratory\nVector Borne Disease Diagnostic Laboratory (VBDDL)\nZoological Oncology and Therapeutics\nClinical Studies Core\nFlow Cytometry and Cell Sorting\nResearch Irradiation Core Facility\nMicroscopy Core Facility\nGenetic Testing\nMolecular Biomedical Sciences\nMolecular Biomedical Sciences\nClinical Pharmacology Laboratory\nPopulation Health and Pathobiology\nPopulation Health and Pathobiology\nAquatic Epidemiology and Conservation\nClinical Microbiology and Molecular Diagnostics\nClinical Pathology\nGastrointestinal Biology and Disease\nHistology\nPoultry Tumor Diseases\nThakur Molecular Epidemiology\nClinical Trials\nClinical Trials\nCats\nDogs\nHorses\nSpecialty: Behavior Services\nSpecialty: Cardiology\nSpecialty: Dermatology\nSpecialty: Internal Medicine\nSpecialty: Nephrology and Urology\nSpecialty: Neurology\nSpecialty: Oncology\nSpecialty: Ophthalmology\nSpecialty: Orthopedics\nSpecialty: Pain Relief and Management\nSpecialty: Surgery\nIndustry Partnerships\nPostdocs\nLAR Contacts\nOutreach\nOutreach\nAlumni\nAlumni\nAlumni Composites\nAlumni Listings\nNC State Community Access Program\nContinuing Education\nCVM Visitor Program\nClinical-Year Externships\nOpen House\nResources\nResources\nHuman Resources\nHuman Resources\nMeet Our CVM HR Staff\nMeet Our Leadership/Staff\nOnboarding\nCommunity Belonging\nEmergency Contacts/Resources\nMental Health Resources\nRewards and Recognition\nTraining Opportunities\nInternational Resources\nFaculty and Staff\nCurrent Students\nCurrent Students\nStudent Development\nStudent Development\nClinical Rotation Dates\nClinical Rotations\nCourse Listings\nDVM Curriculum\nElectives and Selectives\nExtramural Studies\nFocus Areas\nGraduate Student Resources\nAspiring Veterinarians\nDirectory\nLibrary of Veterinary Medicine\nCommunications and Marketing\nCVM IT\nCVM IT\nCVM IT Staff\nCVM Student Laptop Requirements\nHardware Services & Policies\nSoftware Services & Policies\nClassrooms, Teaching Labs & Conference Rooms\nData Security Resources\nSelf Service & FAQs\nCampus Links\nCVM Internal\nInternational Community Resources\nVeterinary Hospital\nEmployers\nEmployers\nPost a Position\nCareer Fairs\nContact Us\nNews\nGive Now\nNow Enrolling Canine Patients with Liver Tumors\nJuly 18, 2023\njldarro2\n2-min. read\nPrinciple Investigator\nDr. Mike Sano\nDescription\nDoes your dog have a liver tumor? We are now enrolling canine patients that have a liver tumor into a clinical trial that is using a new therapy called INSPIRE, which uses electrical pulses to safely destroy the cells within a tumor.\nThis study has two treatment groups.\nOne group of study applicants that have 1-2 liver tumor measuring between 1-8cm will be screened through the Medical Oncology service at NC State Veterinary hospital for eligibility. If eligible, patients in this group will return 1-2 weeks later for a one time INSPIRE therapy treatment. This will be followed by surgery a week later to remove the tumor and part of the liver.\nThe second group of study applicants should have 1-2 liver tumor measuring between 1-8cm. Potential candidates will come in through the Medical Oncology service at NC State Veterinary Hospital for a screening appointment to check eligibility for enrollment. If eligible, patients will return up to 3 times at 3-week intervals for a CT scan and INSPIRE therapy treatment. Once patients have received their last INSPIRE therapy treatment, they will be monitored over a 9 month period which include 5 recheck appointments which include a CT scan and bloodwork.\nTesting Requirements\nPatients should have a cytological diagnosis of the liver tumor prior to their screening appointment.\nEnrollment Start\n07/01/2023\nEnrollment Finish\n07/01/2027\nInclusion Criteria\nPatients have 1-2 liver tumors measuring between 1-8cm\nPatients must weigh at least 30lbs\nPatients must be overall healthy with no other major health concerns\nExclusion Criteria\nMetastasis of the liver tumor or any other forms of cancer\nMajor heart disease or heart arrhythmia’s\nFlyer\nView\nContact\nPlease contact Jewels Darrow at 919-515-5090 or email\n[email protected]\nfor more information.\nCategories:\nclinical_trial\nTags:\nDogs Clinical Trial\nInternal Medicine Clinical Trial\nOncology Clinical Trial\nSurgery Clinical Trial\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nHome\n1060 William Moore Drive\nRaleigh, NC 27607\n919-513-6786\nCAMPUS MAP\nAccessibility\nCopyright\nCommunity and Culture\nMyPack Portal\nDirectory\nLibraries\nJobs\nPolicies\nPrivacy Statement\nContact Us\nConnect With Us\n© 2026 NC State University. All rights reserved.\nAccessibility\nPrivacy\nResources\nClose smart search\nFind NC State websites, locations and people\nSearch this site\nTOP LINKS\nMyPack Portal\nAccess vital records, resources and information for students, families, faculty and staff.\nUniversity Libraries\nOur campus libraries are your destinations for studying, research and expanding your mind.\nAcademic Calendar\nLook up important dates and university holidays for the upcoming academic year and beyond.\nMajors and Careers\nExplore our 300-plus degree programs and see where an NC State education can take you.",
